I also mapped what comes after

The package contains a Phase-4 manifest and twenty concrete continuation targets. The highest-leverage ones are persistent event-sourced Pattern Book/Metamap state, typed real artifacts instead of toy scalar states, deterministic replay, read-only repository adapters, property/fuzz tests, held-out mission benchmarks, calibrated ground-truth metrics, rollback transactions, stale-memory penalties for ROM, Afterglow genealogy, Restoration Spectroscopy, and the Strike-Zone stopping policy.

That last one matters.

The current machine is learning:

\text{which operator should I use?}

The wiser machine learns:

\boxed{
\text{Should I use an operator at all?}
}

So the next maturation isn’t merely more agency.

It’s restraint as agency:

\text{SWING}
\quad|\quad
\text{WATCH}
\quad|\quad
\text{PASS}
\quad|\quad
\text{WAIT}
\quad|\quad
\text{ASK}
\quad|\quad
\text{TEST}

with the strike zone itself recursively calibrated from prediction error and ROM.

That’s where “stop letting life pass you by” gets its useful mirror:

\boxed{\text{Don't let life pass you by—but learn which pitches to let pass.}}

Full ROM means being able to move, including choosing not to.